1→I'll inspect the signed commit, the accepted D.110c-0b0 plan, and the load-bearing implementation/tests as a read-only reviewer.The GREEN ledger and the rest of the commit diff are next; I’ll use those to check the claimed floor/recovery law against the code.I’ll keep going through the remaining diff and the owner-selection/plan records that define the accepted 0b0 law.The floor tests, recovery owner, and accepted 0b0 plan text are the next load-bearing surfaces.I still need the accepted 0b0 owner-selection law and the product hot/cold paths that are supposed to implement it.The accepted owner-selection design and the frozen RED/GREEN rows are the next things to compare against the code.The crash/recovery and classification coverage still looks thin; I’m checking the remaining owners and whether those promised rows actually exist.The remaining gap is whether pending state is reachable through the product’s create/migrate initialization, which I’ll confirm in the open-path checks.{
  "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUIRED",
  "blocking_union_empty": false,
  "p0": [
    {
      "title": "Pending first-transition floor does not dominate product open, so crash recovery can activate the old plane or strand the room",
      "evidence": "Accepted 0b0 law (plan 92515-92530, 92534-92536): after begin-CAS, no old or new generation may activate until recover-then-commit, and pending recovery dominates. examples/v3-room/src/index.ts:1554-1570 only compares floor vs genesis/epoch-1 when pending===null, so a pending 0→1 tuple skips those gates. The genesis branch at 2148-2157 then activateV3LivePlane() with no recoverPendingCreatorSuccessorAdoption. Recovery exists only at 2166-2191 inside the successorSnapshotDeclaration branch. initializeRoomHeadAuthority at 903-912 always create/migrate/read first; a durable create/migrate against {pending, stable:old} conflicts (chat migrate/create at examples/v3-chat/src/index.ts:766-780) instead of completing the pending transition. kind:\"reopen\" is only a type at examples/v3-room/src/index.ts:268; grep shows zero product or test consumers (chat 745-748 and directRoomHeadAuthority at packages/storage-browser/tests/assets/phase-6a-creator-successor-product-entry.ts:817 always create or migrate). Crash after step-3 begin therefore either reactivates the old owner or returns D110C_FLOOR_CONFLICT with no recovery owner.",
      "required_fix": "Before any live activation, if provider state.pending!==null, do not create, migrate, or activate genesis. Drive the existing 0b0a recoverPending path with the pending previous/next tuples, commitRoomHeadAdvance, then activate only after exact dual-owner equality; if successorSnapshotDeclaration is absent or recovery cannot complete, fail closed with D110C_FLOOR_RECOVERY_UNAVAILABLE. Ordinary reopen must read, not create/migrate, and pending must dominate mismatch classification."
    }
10→  ],
  "p1": [
    {
      "title": "GREEN lacks deterministic coverage of the frozen 0b0 crash, classification, create-vs-reopen, and concurrency rows",
      "evidence": "Plan 92606-92632 requires product/provider proof of create-if-never-seen vs refusal to initialize on ordinary reopen (including local epoch 0 → D110C_FLOOR_MIGRATION_REQUIRED), make-before-publish with no activation while pending, every crash row in both AHE orderings, and exact D110C_FLOOR_* mutants (stale/forked/skipped/duplicate/cross-object/cross-genesis/regressed/malformed/missing/unavailable/concurrent). tests/phase-6b-d110c-0b0-floor-red.test.ts:16-61 is one Node-child test for missing/wrong/correct expectedRoomHead. 0b0a tests cover the Node stage/recover seam only. No test asserts D110C_FLOOR_UNAVAILABLE, CONFLICT, REGRESSION, PENDING_INVALID, HEAD_AHEAD, or RECOVERY_UNAVAILABLE, product six-step order, used-scope non-reuse, or participant advanced reopen without a pin. kind:\"reopen\" has no executable consumer.",
      "required_fix": "Add deterministic product+provider tests for each frozen crash row (both AHE orderings), create-if-never-seen vs reopen missing-scope including epoch 0, the full classification matrix, concurrent begin-CAS, and in-process six-step order with no old/new activation while pending. Do not treat 0b0a Node tests or source-contains checks as covering those rows."
    },
    {
      "title": "Open-path HEAD_AHEAD vs MISMATCH codes are inverted relative to the frozen table",
      "evidence": "Plan 92538-92562: HEAD_AHEAD is reserved for an authenticated room head ahead of the stable floor with no pending; MISMATCH is floor ahead of room or otherwise different without an exact pending selector. examples/v3-room/src/index.ts:1559-1560 emits HEAD_AHEAD when openedRoomHeadState.stable.epoch > genesis (floor ahead of the genesis tuple being opened). 1563-1568 emits MISMATCH for successorSnapshotDeclaration when stable.epoch!==1, including floor epoch 0 behind an epoch-1 successor open. Both still fail closed, but the frozen codes have different prescribed handling and no test distinguishes them.",
20→      "required_fix": "Classify only after pending domination and comparison of the copied stable floor to the authenticated room head: HEAD_AHEAD iff room is ahead and pending is null; MISMATCH iff floor is ahead or otherwise differs without an exact pending selector. Cover both rows with exact-code tests."
    }
  ],
  "p2": [
    {
      "title": "Room-head capture does not bind scope.pinnedGenesisAnchorDigest, so cross-genesis provider values are not D110C_FLOOR_INVALID at the room boundary",
      "evidence": "Plan 92549: cross-genesis provider value is D110C_FLOOR_INVALID. captureRoomHeadState at examples/v3-room/src/index.ts:310-327 checks objectId and pending epoch+1/digest inequality but never pinnedGenesisAnchorDigest. A well-shaped same-objectId head from another genesis can pass capture and later fail Node equality as D110C_FLOOR_MISMATCH (packages/node/src/creator-adoption-activate.ts:249-250, 286-287).",
      "disposition": "In the 0b0 correction, reject captured state as D110C_FLOOR_INVALID unless epoch-0 currentAnchorDigest equals scope.pinnedGenesisAnchorDigest (and pending previous carries that binding). Do not wait for D.110c-a/b."
    }
  ],
30→  "summary": "Node cold missing/wrong/correct expectedRoomHead closes the causal RED, and hot verify→stage→begin→publish→commit→activate plus successor pending recovery are present, but pending does not dominate product open: genesis reopen can activate the old plane, create/migrate can strand a correct pending room, and the frozen crash/classification/create-vs-reopen proof list is untested. Fable a/b predicate-closure and 0b1 predecessor-floor retention P1s stay prospective and do not reopen 0b0."
}

